---
description: Rube Goldberg Hello World project rules for Cursor
globs:
  - "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root before making changes and follow it.

- Milestone-driven development: one milestone at a time per
  `docs/architecture.md` section 29; track scope and acceptance in
  `docs/implementation-status.md`.
- Required gates (must all pass): `make format`, `make lint`, `make unit`,
  `make coverage`, `make build`. Missing toolchains are skipped unless
  `STRICT=1`.
- Non-negotiable integrity rules: only the CLI, orchestrator, and glyph
  catalog may see the requested plaintext; downstream events must never
  contain `targetText`, `expectedCharacter`, `unicodeCodePoint`, or
  equivalent fields (`docs/architecture.md` section 7).
- Pin all dependency and container versions; never use `latest` tags.
- Do not combine service languages; do not bypass required protocols
  (REST, SOAP, gRPC, Kafka, SSE).
- Do not add explanatory comments; write idiomatic code and keep it
  readable.
- Never commit unless explicitly authorized.
